commit 1f7ba2b2b3c0316550163a0ae38a05482c97c797
Author: admin <admin@MacBook-Pro-de-admin.local>
Date:   Mon Aug 24 14:32:07 2026 -0400

    feat: migrate all 54 markets onto RammRegistry, verified end-to-end
    
    Completes the registry migration started earlier this session:
    deployed RammRegistry (0x7a5138a6371aa21c384d100fa7d7ef2be2c552d4) pointed
    at the existing, unchanged RAMMToken/RedemptionNFT/VestingVault/
    PromoStaking, then redeployed PVTToken+IMPXMarket for all 41 demo
    products and 13 brand campaigns against the new registry-aware
    constructor.
    
    Found and fixed a real bug in the process, not just re-ran the old
    scripts: deployDemoProducts.ts only wrote productContracts.ts once at
    the very end of the loop. The first migration attempt hit Base's public
    RPC rate limit (a shared, free endpoint under real load from 40+
    sequential product deployments) and crashed after 38/41 products had
    already deployed on-chain — with zero record of their addresses saved
    anywhere. Fixed properly before re-running: viem's http() transport now
    retries with backoff (retryCount: 10, retryDelay: 3000) on all five bulk
    scripts (deployDemoProducts, migrateCampaignContracts,
    seedMarketLiquidity, seedCampaignLiquidity, auditOwnership), and
    productContracts.ts/campaigns.json now checkpoint-write after every
    single product/campaign instead of once at the end.
    
    (Deliberately did NOT add "skip already-deployed" resume logic —
    productContracts.ts always has *some* entry per product from whichever
    deployment generation last succeeded, so treating "key present" as
    "done" would silently skip products that genuinely need redeploying.
    The incremental-write fix protects against losing a crash's progress;
    it doesn't try to make re-runs skip real work.)
    
    Verified for real, not just via the migration scripts' own log lines
    (this session already proved once that a logged "success" can lie —
    see the 31/49 silent transferOwnership failure from earlier):
    - auditOwnership.ts: 0/54 products have wrong PVTToken ownership
    - auditRegistry.ts (new): RammRegistry's own four pointers correct,
      and all 54 markets' registry() call resolves to the right address
    - Real end-to-end buy + sell against a freshly-migrated market
      (agatha), both transactions confirmed on-chain
    
    Also updated app/constants/env.ts's legacy single PVT_ADDRESS/
    MARKET_ADDRESS fallback to the fresh agatha addresses.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

